# Aus Daves Installationsband extrahiert, reproduzierbar
work/kreiss-newasm/

# Gate runs: obj_<label>/ is 5,528 decks and <label>.tsv is their hashes.
# Reproducible from tools/gate.sh in ten minutes, and 30 MB each.  A single
# `git add -A` from the repo root put 11,565 of them into one commit on
# 2026-09-10 and took .git from 92 MB to 131 MB.
obj_*/
/modules.txt

# The repository root is scratch for gate runs: every <label>.tsv beside an
# obj_<label>/ is 5,528 hashes from a ten-minute run.  The pattern used to be
# /g[0-9]*.tsv and /r[0-9]*.tsv, which caught g343 and missed gblank, amaclib,
# tattrexpr and twenty more -- a label is a word, not a number.  Measurements
# that are meant to be kept live under work/measurements/, never here.
/*.tsv
work/measurements/dlib-bytes/
work/measurements/amvssrc-tk5*/

# Credentials -- see .env.example and tools/creds.py
.env

# The three-source-state run: the pinned binaries and the symlink tree are
# reproducible, PROVENANCE.txt is the part that must survive.
work/src-states/bin/as370
work/src-states/bin/cmplmd370
work/src-states/applied/
